) & =F(-x) \\\\  & =(-x)^{3}-(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315079 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315079 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315079 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315079 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=5{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c31042af-d0b1-56e0-8fc6-7b7b6e402e06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315079 #edb/ref 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=5{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}+2x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315081 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315081 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315081 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315081 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1a98a94-1685-5290-8055-415073e9036d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315081 #edb/ref 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{6(\\sqrt{3}-2)}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372764 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372764 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372764 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372764 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-4x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{n}.$\n\n$\\,{a}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}\nfor $n\\ge 1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372764 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac7731e8-df1e-5709-a827-9379c5eafbc5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372764 #edb/ref 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-4x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{8}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{8}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{n\\pi }(0+\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{8(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi ))}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{8(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186372769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372765 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a167a142-5a35-5de0-bf3c-bfdf6ad5f747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372766 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{8(1+(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372766 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372766 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e18a8cac-f51a-57be-9cc2-c525c3637b17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372767 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{8(1-(-1)^{n})}{4\\pi {n}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372767 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372767 #edb/ref 1083 #u